# Ordered XNU patches shared by every SDM710 port, one path per line.
#
# Both patches are carried for context parity with the series UniXNU applies, not for their
# board functionality. Upstream keeps them next to its SM8550 patches instead of in the ARM64
# or OS series, and those series assume they are present.
#
# native-smp-secondary: the BCM2837 (4 KiB) personality starts at MAX_CPUS = 4 and numbers its
# cores in Affinity0; SDM710 has eight cores numbered in Affinity1 (0x000..0x700). Without this
# patch the kernel caps at four CPUs and computes the wrong CPU number on secondary start.
native-smp-secondary.patch

# sheng-platform-power: adds the XNU_SHENG_PMGR call block to bsd_init.c. The OS series patch
# zzz-boot-progress.patch was exported against that context and does not apply without it.
# CONFIG_XNU_SHENG_PMGR is off in this port, so the block compiles to nothing.
sheng-platform-power.patch
